# Commit Clean — No --no-verify

- **Never use `git commit --no-verify`** (or `-n`). All commits must pass the pre-commit hook.
- Fix lint and formatting before committing:
  - Run `pnpm exec lint-staged` (or stage files and let the hook run on commit).
  - Resolve all ESLint errors and Prettier issues in staged files.
- If the hook fails, fix the reported problems (e.g. in `integrations.ts`: complexity, max-depth, naming). Use targeted `eslint-disable-next-line` with a short justification only when refactoring is deferred; prefer fixing the rule.
- Ensure TypeScript compiles and tests pass before committing.
